{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/828484-fetches-in-the-hedge","id":828484,"title":"Fetches in the Hedge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-11T16:10:40-08:00","id":828484,"title":"Fetches in the Hedge?","content":"After a player of mine asked an interesting question, I flipped through Autumn Nightmares and the Core looking for any information about Fetches in the Hedge, and I found nothing. So, I'm going to the community to ask if there are any kind of special considerations that might affect a Fetch?<br /> If there's any published information I missed, I'd appreciate if someone could point it out. Otherwise, I'd be thrilled to hear any interesting ideas for plot hooks or mechanical considerations that you might have.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I'm thinking that it should be more obvious what a Fetch is - that whatever makes them appear human is similar to the Mask, and is at least weakened in the Hedge. Also that the portions of the soul they have (manifested by a shadow, or other symbolic features) can be easily frayed away by the Thorns, reducing them to an automaton. Likely, also, that the Hedge psychoactively reacts to them having not-quite-human minds and emotions, distorting in bizarre and menacing ways.<br /> <br /> What other fun things might you all do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T16:13:41-08:00","id":828486,"title":"","content":"Yeah I had this same problem. I believe my solution was they became strawmen and trinkety hobgoblins after spending too much time. After all they don't even have seemings they always look human until after death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T16:23:36-08:00","id":828492,"title":"","content":"The only relevant information I can recall is that Fetches cannot open Hedgegates by default, they need to posses the right Echo, so in a lot of cases even getting into the Hedge might be tricky for a fetch. I think the weakened mask thing sounds right, although I don't remember there being clear rules on how easy it is to spot a fetch in the first place. There are lines here and there implying that Changelings can see through a fetch's mask, unless the fetch possesses the normalcy echo, but I don't know if they do so automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:22:58-08:00","id":828551,"title":"","content":"There might be some missing the point.<br /> <br /> Fetches in the Hedge operate as humans do-they have Morality/Integrity, after all. Further, in the interest of them being a wall to keep changelings from comfortably going back, there's actually relatively little reason to have the Fetch react in any particular way to the Hedge beyond some of it's Echoes. If there is a fae creature that belongs to Ironside, it's fetches.<br /> <br /> Fetches don't drop their 'mask' for anything short of death. In this way, they are still more 'you' than you are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T07:22:51-08:00","id":828772,"title":"","content":"I realize its not really part of the scope of the average game. My chronicle is gong ... interesting places, and I have to wiggle the themes and come up with interesting answers now and then.<br /> <br /> For context: my player's changeling fell in love with the girl next door, learned she was a Fetch when the changeling escaped and started coming after her, and decided to stay with the Fetch. Because I like drama, and my players like bad decisions. <br /> They fought, as they tend to; the changeling won, and my player stepped in to spare the Fetch with a, &quot;its your life; take it back, just don't kill her and she'll leave you alone&quot; compromise. <br /> His next terrible idea is to hide the Fetch in his hollow until she can get on her feet again with a new life or whatever.<br /> <br /> So, this is clearly an outlandish situation which, while it fits the Sympathy For The Fetch portrayal, requires a lot of alteration to the themes, and now leaves me to consider if anything particular should come up with a Fetch in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> I doubt my situation will be seen in another chronicle, but there are other situations I could imagine: a Fetch's counterattack chasing a Changeling into the Hedge, or even, like the sample character in Autumn Nightmares, a Fetch in a goblin market, seeking fae magics for a &quot;cure&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, I will take your point a little askew to investigate what kind of themes I Am using Fetches for in my chronicle, and see if I can highlight those...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:35:43-08:00","id":828889,"title":"","content":"Is the fetch's changeling a PC or frequent NPC?<br /> <br /> Because if that's the case, I would have the fetch be a knife in the heart even after giving up her home, namely by playing up the innocence of the character in contrast to the changeling. After all, the changeling knows things now that most fetches just can't-though said fetch gets some of it now. Her humanity in response to her loss of home and the Hedge could do a great job with making all changelings involved ask themselves whether this is fair or right, whether they're monsters(they are, but that's not the point) or not. Use the fetch to create a sense of the changelings involved making a Durance in micro-form.<br /> <br /> Now, if said changeling is not in the picture, then I can see how the degrading thing goes, but you have two directions to go here still. One is, I feel, a little more true to Changeling, but the other does have appeal. The first one is don't change the face-change the self beyond the face. Let that innocence warp and twist, let her become manipulative and exploitative, let her emotions become longer and poisoned. Make it seem like a natural extension of her trauma-after all, it is in some way. And make it clear-she could be better if she were anchored in reality where she belongs. Trips to the mall should show her virtues more strongly, while the Hedge, well, brings her to vice again and again. Let her keep the face you know, but turn her into a tortured muse for the PC's. It's a different kind of breakdown, one that holds true to the fetch and changelings<br /> <br /> The second is the one y'all are talking about, where the fetch breaks down. I like the aesthetic, and I like it separate from the other one because it just makes it tragic. The fetch only has so long to live without time in the mortal world. It's simple, it's straightforward. But it doesn't play into Lost's themes as nicely as some might think. To fix that up a little, consider not only letting the body degenerate, but also letting the personality degenerate. Not in the same way as the last paragraph, but like a toy as it's batteries slowly give out. Not only the does doing anything become harder for the fetch to do, but her humor slips out, her wit dulls, her charm and sexuality burns out. Less and less a person, until she's just a doll, and then not even that.<br /> <br /> One final option to consider is to let her start warping to become the relevant PC's fetch. Well, maybe in a really long run, that exactly, but instead, just warp the fetch to make it so that it uses elements of the person she replaced to make the changeling feel like they have no place in the world, even in the Hedge. And this can get really weird and messed up if you let that extend to physical stuff, though that's a little too messy for me to suggest on.<br /> <br /> I dunno, some thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T13:29:07-08:00","id":828935,"title":"","content":"Those are all fantastic ideas. I definitely think I will go with the personality devolving into spiteful, poisoned driftwood. It actually ties into broader complications and themes the chronicle is focusing on. I'm still considering a few physical changes, but I just like physical representations like that.<br /> <br /> Both the Fetch and her changeling are NPCs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:58:23-08:00","id":828968,"title":"","content":"Hm, I remember there being a couple of Fetches in 1st edition that eventually started deteriorating even without anyone trying to kill them. Eugene from the Rites of Spring prologue had some out of control cancer they were hoping to cure with a Hera Pear, and Don Sarno from Autumn Nightmares started turning back to splintered wood as the magic that bound him together waned. Neither of these were tied to the Hedge though, it was just presented as a thing that sometimes happens to Fetches. <br /> <br /> My fetch in my first Changeling game basically committed suicide by Autumn Court for that exact reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:11:27-08:00","id":828974,"title":"","content":"The cancer was just cancer (just, he says). As for Don Sarno, sure, but there's rules and there are exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}